    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b3deb4ed",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: r.i.p_trayvon_martin; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman standing beside a large portrait of Trayvon Martin, a Black teenager fatally shot in 2012, with the text 'r.i.p. trayvon martin' overlaid. The scene is presented in a gallery-like setting, suggesting a commemorative or memorial context. The overall intent is to honor Trayvon Martin's memory and draw attention to racial injustice and the broader social movement surrounding his death. The meme does not contain abusive, cyberbullying, misogynistic, or propagandistic elements. However, it is inherently harmful because it evokes the trauma and systemic racism associated with his death, potentially retraumatizing victims' families and communities. The juxtaposition of the portrait with the text serves as a visual memorial, aiming to provoke reflection and solidarity, but the context of the image—being a portrait of a victim of racial violence—can be emotionally distressing and may contribute to the perpetuation of trauma narratives. The intent is not to attack or demean, but to memorialize and raise awareness, which, while not hateful, is still a form of harmful content due to its association with a violent and racially charged historical event.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f22d6762"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
