      "instance_name": "mapping_r_i_p_trayvon_martin_to_portrait",
      "label": "Text memorializes the subject of the portrait",
      "description": "The text 'r.i.p. trayvon martin' is overlaid on the image and directly refers to the person depicted in the large portrait. The portrait visually represents Trayvon Martin, and the text explicitly identifies him as the subject of the memorial. This creates an analogical mapping where the textual entity 'r.i.p. trayvon martin' is mapped onto the visual entity 'portrait' (specifically, the portrait of Trayvon Martin). The text serves to label and contextualize the visual material, establishing a direct semantic link between the memorial text and the visual representation of the deceased individual.",
